# Git hooks — no --no-verify

Never run `git commit --no-verify`, `git push --no-verify`, or any other git command with `--no-verify` / `-n` to skip hooks.

This applies even when hooks fail due to environment issues (missing Ruby, bundler, mapfile, etc.).

## When hooks fail

1. Fix the underlying issue (code, RuboCop offenses, failing specs, hook script bugs).
2. If the agent environment cannot run hooks, **stop and tell the user** — do not bypass.
3. Ask the user to commit/push locally, or to explicitly approve skipping hooks in their message if they accept the risk.

## Allowed only when

The user **explicitly** writes in the same message that hooks may be skipped, e.g. "commit with --no-verify" or "skip pre-commit for this commit".

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ Never (unless user explicitly requested skip in this message)
git commit --no-verify -m "..."
git push --no-verify

# ✅ Fix offenses, then commit normally
bundle exec rubocop -A path/to/file.rb
git commit -m "..."

# ✅ Or ask the user to commit locally when hooks cannot run here
```
